flowchart TB
    accTitle: Trajectory processing pipeline
    accDescr: Source GPS data is parsed and preserved as original trajectories, normalised into uniformed trajectories, then cleaned with rule-based filters and gap splitting to produce cleaned trajectories. A per-query stage extracts subtrajectories between two regions, clusters similar paths, and returns representative routes with traversal counts.

    subgraph ingest[1 . Ingestion]
        direction LR
        og[Source GPS dataset<br/>Porto / Beijing / upload]
        parse[Parse and preserve<br/>raw observations]
        storeOriginal[(Original<br/>trajectories)]
        og --> parse --> storeOriginal
    end

    subgraph transform[2 . Normalise and clean]
        direction LR
        normalise[Normalise to<br/>common schema]
        storeUniformed[(Uniformed<br/>trajectories)]
        clean[Rule-based cleaning<br/>+ gap splitting]
        storeCleaned[(Cleaned<br/>trajectories)]
        normalise --> storeUniformed --> clean --> storeCleaned
    end

    subgraph querypipe[3 . Per-query route pipeline]
        direction LR
        params[Query input:<br/>entry, exit, time, similarity]
        extract[Extract<br/>subtrajectories]
        cluster[Cluster into<br/>route groups]
        output[Representative routes:<br/>counts, IDs, timestamps]
        params --> extract --> cluster --> output
    end

    ingest --> transform --> querypipe

    classDef input fill:#fff4cc,stroke:#76520e,color:#2c2109,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef process fill:#e9f8ef,stroke:#237a46,color:#123d26,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef store fill:#f4eafe,stroke:#7446a6,color:#35204d,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef output fill:#e8f1ff,stroke:#245ea8,color:#102a43,stroke-width:1.5px;

    class og,params input;
    class parse,normalise,clean,extract,cluster process;
    class storeOriginal,storeUniformed,storeCleaned store;
    class output output;